{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "0H23", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$x$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-factor-through-residual-space}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{lemma-factor-through-residual-space-Noetherian}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:81ca23c16f1bf9b0e20841c2c2d6365662c2dc10a7c65a91ce682bacdbf04da5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5a298e558197eb16ac01afc41ca6b45146edeefeb21c7fa77abb71f0e00589b6", "source_text": "We do not know whether Lemma <REF_0001>\nholds if we only assume <MATH_0001> is locally Noetherian, i.e., we\ndrop the assumption on the inertia being quasi-compact. In this case,\nif <MATH_0002> is a closed point, this is certainly true as follows from the\nfollowing much simpler lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b1238e8fa5e450f8463963442fd8664e66a5f0e119c06a6624afeb79b28f8c2a", "unit_id": "tag:0H26:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0H23", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z}_x \\subset \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$x$", "MATH_0005": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{Z}_x \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-every-point-residual-gerbe-locally-Noetherian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-residual-space-closed}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1d4ad0417c9dde8bdf951cb61b1c807a623fc9f71ab25fecfb62da4640c6ed7d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b5e425cb3b5f4844a60e424d54ab7a05bb9571f19f764abf880290131c18e92a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian algebraic stack.\nLet <MATH_0002> with residual gerbe\n<MATH_0003>\n(Lemma <REF_0001>).\nThen <MATH_0004> is a closed point of <MATH_0005> if and only if\nthe morphism <MATH_0006> is a closed immersion.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:842b8afbd011029ecce4529a60792f90c97aabc40d298d3232098193f437ca92", "unit_id": "tag:0H27:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0H23", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{Z}_x \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$x$", "MATH_0003": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0004": "$x$", "MATH_0005": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\subset \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$|Z| = \\{x\\}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0010": "$|\\mathcal{Z}| = \\{x\\}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{Z} = \\mathcal{Z}_x$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-closed-immersion-proper}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{stacks-properties-lemma-reduced-closed-substack}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-immersion-locally-finite-type}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-locally-finite-type-locally-noetherian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a2159133e9f8126cd29eccaff141e2a9389b9a6336e72394b27529de5b870193", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ca24ebe8b4e776e7c0d824275db2e0bbd97ea193b5eed123c05b7b8ecc972332", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is a closed immersion, then\n<MATH_0002> is a closed point of <MATH_0003>, see for example\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nConversely, assume <MATH_0004> is a closed point of <MATH_0005>.\nLet <MATH_0006>\nbe the reduced closed substack with <MATH_0007>\n(Properties of Stacks,\nLemma <REF_0002>).\nThen <MATH_0008> is a locally Noetherian algebraic stack\nby Lemmas <REF_0003> and\n<REF_0004>.\nSince also <MATH_0009> is reduced and <MATH_0010>\nit follows that <MATH_0011> is the\nresidual gerbe by definition.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:17ab6ccf9a63d8f2e58161f44dc5a98e30d0f4d8539e068eaac7208a88dd2286", "unit_id": "tag:0H27:proof"}
